\newlabel{tab:codec-comparison}{{2}{8}{\textbf {Realized size ratio by input and codec.} Values are encoded bytes divided by raw UTF-8 bytes and reported as percentages; lower is better. AC payload excludes the Qwen container and is shown only for cost attribution. All remaining entries are complete, round-trip-verified streams, and bold marks the smallest complete stream per row}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Tokenizer fertility on the held-out 5\,MB text8 test region (855{,}233 whitespace-delimited words). The text8 BPE is trained only on the first 90\,MB with a 32k vocabulary. Fertility is tokens per word (lower is better); bytes per token is the compression-oriented inverse (higher is better). All tokenizers reconstruct the input exactly. The domain-trained BPE produces 4.4\% fewer tokens than Qwen.}}{8}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:tokenizer-fertility}{{3}{8}{Tokenizer fertility on the held-out 5\,MB text8 test region (855{,}233 whitespace-delimited words). The text8 BPE is trained only on the first 90\,MB with a 32k vocabulary. Fertility is tokens per word (lower is better); bytes per token is the compression-oriented inverse (higher is better). All tokenizers reconstruct the input exactly. The domain-trained BPE produces 4.4\% fewer tokens than Qwen}{table.3}{}}
